{"id":"86d78681ff9eb573","group":"58","path":"58/batch19/58-thm-kolmogorov-chains.md","title":"Kolmogorov's Extension Theorem","display":"thm-kolmogorov-chains — Kolmogorov's Extension Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-kolmogorov-chains","aliases":["58-thm-kolmogorov-chains"],"display":"thm-kolmogorov-chains — Kolmogorov's Extension Theorem","depends_on":["[[58-df-zfc-measure8-standard-borel-space]]","[[58-df-zfc-measure6-probability-measure]]","[[58-df-function]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-kolmogorov-chains"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-kolmogorov-chains</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-kolmogorov-chains — Kolmogorov's Extension Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"2bc25b4a67d5fe1e\" href=\"?note=2bc25b4a67d5fe1e\" title=\"58-df-zfc-measure8-standard-borel-space\">58-df-zfc-measure8-standard-borel-space</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"29e8d6cd15d08f4f\" href=\"?note=29e8d6cd15d08f4f\" title=\"58-df-zfc-measure6-probability-measure\">58-df-zfc-measure6-probability-measure</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"58-df-function\">58-df-function</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Explicit relation signatures used below: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Function}\\subseteq V^{3}\">\\(\\operatorname{Function}\\subseteq V^{3}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MeasureStandardBorel}_S\\subseteq V^{2}\">\\(\\mathrm{MeasureStandardBorel}_S\\subseteq V^{2}\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure6ProbabilityMeasure}_S\\subseteq V^{3}\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure6ProbabilityMeasure}_S\\subseteq V^{3}\\)</span>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"I\\in V\">\\(I\\in V\\)</span> (index set)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"E,\\Sigma\\in V\">\\(E,\\Sigma\\in V\\)</span> are set-coded functions on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"I\">\\(I\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"(E_i,\\Sigma_i)=(E(i),\\Sigma(i))\">\\((E_i,\\Sigma_i)=(E(i),\\Sigma(i))\\)</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MeasureStandardBorel}_S(E_i,\\Sigma_i)\">\\(\\mathrm{MeasureStandardBorel}_S(E_i,\\Sigma_i)\\)</span> is the standard-Borel predicate</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mu\\in V\">\\(\\mu\\in V\\)</span> is a set-coded function on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"[I]^{&lt;\\omega}\">\\([I]^{&lt;\\omega}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mu_F=\\mu(F)\">\\(\\mu_F=\\mu(F)\\)</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure6ProbabilityMeasure}_S(X,\\mathcal A,\\nu)\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure6ProbabilityMeasure}_S(X,\\mathcal A,\\nu)\\)</span> is the probability-measure predicate</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\pi_F^G:\\prod_{i\\in G}E_i\\to\\prod_{i\\in F}E_i\">\\(\\pi_F^G:\\prod_{i\\in G}E_i\\to\\prod_{i\\in F}E_i\\)</span> is the coordinate projection for <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F\\subseteq G\\subseteq I\">\\(F\\subseteq G\\subseteq I\\)</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}kolmogorov\\text{-}chains}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\operatorname{Function}(E,I,\\operatorname{ran}(E))\n\\land\\operatorname{Function}(\\Sigma,I,\\operatorname{ran}(\\Sigma))\n\\land\\forall i\\in I\\;\\mathrm{MeasureStandardBorel}_S(E_i,\\Sigma_i)\n\\land\\operatorname{Function}(\\mu,[I]^{&lt;\\omega},\\operatorname{ran}(\\mu))\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall F\\in[I]^{&lt;\\omega}\\;\n\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure6ProbabilityMeasure}_S\\!\\left(\\prod_{i\\in F}E_i,\\bigotimes_{i\\in F}\\Sigma_i,\\mu_F\\right)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall F,G\\in[I]^{&lt;\\omega}\\;\\bigl(F\\subseteq G\\to(\\pi_F^G)_*\\mu_G=\\mu_F\\bigr)\\\\\n&amp;\\to\\exists!\\mathbb P\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure6ProbabilityMeasure}_S\\!\\left(\\prod_{i\\in I}E_i,\\bigotimes_{i\\in I}\\Sigma_i,\\mathbb P\\right)\n\\land\\forall F\\in[I]^{&lt;\\omega}\\;(\\pi_F^I)_*\\mathbb P=\\mu_F\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}kolmogorov\\text{-}chains}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\operatorname{Function}(E,I,\\operatorname{ran}(E))\n\\land\\operatorname{Function}(\\Sigma,I,\\operatorname{ran}(\\Sigma))\n\\land\\forall i\\in I\\;\\mathrm{MeasureStandardBorel}_S(E_i,\\Sigma_i)\n\\land\\operatorname{Function}(\\mu,[I]^{&lt;\\omega},\\operatorname{ran}(\\mu))\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall F\\in[I]^{&lt;\\omega}\\;\n\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure6ProbabilityMeasure}_S\\!\\left(\\prod_{i\\in F}E_i,\\bigotimes_{i\\in F}\\Sigma_i,\\mu_F\\right)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall F,G\\in[I]^{&lt;\\omega}\\;\\bigl(F\\subseteq G\\to(\\pi_F^G)_*\\mu_G=\\mu_F\\bigr)\\\\\n&amp;\\to\\exists!\\mathbb P\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure6ProbabilityMeasure}_S\\!\\left(\\prod_{i\\in I}E_i,\\bigotimes_{i\\in I}\\Sigma_i,\\mathbb P\\right)\n\\land\\forall F\\in[I]^{&lt;\\omega}\\;(\\pi_F^I)_*\\mathbb P=\\mu_F\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The three indexing families are genuine set-coded functions with set-valued ranges; the former map-class notation incorrectly used the proper class <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"V\">\\(V\\)</span> as a codomain.  Probability typing and projective consistency are explicit, and no Markov property or transition matrix is required.</li>\n<li>Kolmogorov's theorem constructs stochastic processes.</li>\n<li>It ensures existence from consistent specifications.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-zfc-measure8-standard-borel-space","status":"resolved","id":"2bc25b4a67d5fe1e","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-zfc-measure8-standard-borel-space]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-zfc-measure6-probability-measure","status":"resolved","id":"29e8d6cd15d08f4f","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-zfc-measure6-probability-measure]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-function","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-function]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\operatorname{Function}\\subseteq V^{3}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{MeasureStandardBorel}_S\\subseteq V^{2}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure6ProbabilityMeasure}_S\\subseteq V^{3}","display":false},{"tex":"I\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"E,\\Sigma\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"I","display":false},{"tex":"(E_i,\\Sigma_i)=(E(i),\\Sigma(i))","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{MeasureStandardBorel}_S(E_i,\\Sigma_i)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mu\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"[I]^{<\\omega}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mu_F=\\mu(F)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure6ProbabilityMeasure}_S(X,\\mathcal A,\\nu)","display":false},{"tex":"\\pi_F^G:\\prod_{i\\in G}E_i\\to\\prod_{i\\in F}E_i","display":false},{"tex":"F\\subseteq G\\subseteq I","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}kolmogorov\\text{-}chains}\\vdash{}&\n\\operatorname{Function}(E,I,\\operatorname{ran}(E))\n\\land\\operatorname{Function}(\\Sigma,I,\\operatorname{ran}(\\Sigma))\n\\land\\forall i\\in I\\;\\mathrm{MeasureStandardBorel}_S(E_i,\\Sigma_i)\n\\land\\operatorname{Function}(\\mu,[I]^{<\\omega},\\operatorname{ran}(\\mu))\\\\\n&\\land\\forall F\\in[I]^{<\\omega}\\;\n\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure6ProbabilityMeasure}_S\\!\\left(\\prod_{i\\in F}E_i,\\bigotimes_{i\\in F}\\Sigma_i,\\mu_F\\right)\\\\\n&\\land\\forall F,G\\in[I]^{<\\omega}\\;\\bigl(F\\subseteq G\\to(\\pi_F^G)_*\\mu_G=\\mu_F\\bigr)\\\\\n&\\to\\exists!\\mathbb P\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{ZfcMeasure6ProbabilityMeasure}_S\\!\\left(\\prod_{i\\in I}E_i,\\bigotimes_{i\\in I}\\Sigma_i,\\mathbb P\\right)\n\\land\\forall F\\in[I]^{<\\omega}\\;(\\pi_F^I)_*\\mathbb P=\\mu_F\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"V","display":false}],"bytes":2319,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4254","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch19/58-thm-kolmogorov-chains.md|58-thm-kolmogorov-chains]]（batch19）"}],"outgoing":["2bc25b4a67d5fe1e","29e8d6cd15d08f4f","36d7463d215be751"]}